{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/focussystem"]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Navigate between interactive elements using the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Focus System","role":"article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TUIkit provides a focus system that lets users move between interactive views (buttons, menus, text fields) using Tab, Shift+Tab, or arrow keys. The system consists of three parts:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]},{"text":": Tracks which element is focused, handles navigation","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Protocol that views adopt to receive focus","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","isActive":true}]},{"type":"text","text":": Lightweight state object that views use to query and request focus"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"How-Focus-Works","level":2,"text":"How Focus Works"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every frame, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"},{"type":"text","text":" is cleared and interactive views re-register themselves during rendering. This means focus registrations are always in sync with the current view tree: removed views are automatically unregistered."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The focus order follows the rendering order: the first focusable view rendered is first in the Tab cycle."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Focusable-Protocol","level":2,"text":"The Focusable Protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Views that want to receive focus conform to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public protocol Focusable: AnyObject {","    var focusID: String { get }","    var canBeFocused: Bool { get }","    func onFocusReceived()","    func onFocusLost()","    func handleKeyEvent(_ event: KeyEvent) -> Bool","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"focusID","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Unique identifier for this focusable element","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canBeFocused"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Whether focus can move to this element (default: "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"onFocusReceived()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element gains focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"onFocusLost()","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Called when this element loses focus (default: no-op)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Handle a key event while focused; return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" if consumed"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A default extension provides sensible defaults for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canBeFocused"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusReceived()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFocusLost()"},{"type":"text","text":" (both no-ops). Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"focusID"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" must be implemented."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Using-FocusState","level":2,"text":"Using FocusState"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the user-facing API for checking and requesting focus inside a view:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let focusState = FocusState(id: \"my-button\", focusManager: context.environment.focusManager)","","\/\/ Check if this element is currently focused","if focusState.isFocused {","    \/\/ render with focus indicator","}","","\/\/ Programmatically request focus","focusState.requestFocus()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in views like ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Menu","isActive":true},{"text":" create their own ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" internally: you only need it when building custom focusable views.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Navigation-Keys","level":2,"text":"Navigation Keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"},{"type":"text","text":" responds to these keys during dispatch:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the next element"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shift+Tab"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow Down \/ Right"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Move focus to the next element","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow Up \/ Left","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Move focus to the previous element"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"FocusRegistration-Helper","level":2,"text":"FocusRegistration Helper"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Built-in interactive views use the internal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"text":" helper to avoid boilerplate. It handles three tasks in one call:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist a focus ID"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" via ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateStorage","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it remains stable across renders","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Register","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the handler with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"FocusManager","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Query"}]},{"type":"text","text":" whether this view currently has focus"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom views that implement "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Focusable"},{"type":"text","text":" typically do not need "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusRegistration"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. It is used by the framework’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_*Core"},{"type":"text","text":" views (e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_ButtonCore"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_ListCore"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Focus-Indicator","level":2,"text":"Focus Indicator"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The visual indicator depends on the view type. Buttons and similar controls use a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"highlight background bar"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for the focused item. Text fields use "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"pulsing vertical bars","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (caps) around the input area. Lists and tables use a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"highlight background"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for the focused row, with a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pulsing accent background"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when the row is both focused and selected."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Focus-in-the-Event-Loop","level":2,"text":"Focus in the Event Loop"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Focus dispatch happens in Layer 2 of the key event pipeline (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A key event arrives from stdin","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 1 (status bar) gets first chance to handle it"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer 2: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyEventDispatcher"},{"type":"text","text":" dispatches to the focused view’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleKeyEvent(_:)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If not consumed, navigation keys (Tab, arrows) are handled by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FocusManager"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Layer 3 (default bindings) handles quit, theme cycling, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ImageDecoding"],"generated":true}],"references":{"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/CustomViews":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build your own views by composing existing ones or creating custom view modifiers."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/customviews","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Custom Views","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/StatusBarGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"S